# ER042 Normalized Capture — Flagship-and-Orbit Publication Audit 4

## Receipt status

Complete substantive capture of the fourth publication-strategy audit. ER042 formalizes the minimum-paper problem under completeness, proof integrity, audience fit, length, and coherent-question constraints; endorses a five-paper flagship-and-orbit architecture; rejects mega-supplements; recommends audience-specific journal routing; preserves gate-dependent Papers 6–7; and warns that Paper 2 may need a theorem-class split if its complete proof corpus exceeds a realistic article length.

## Main recommendations

1. Treat the five-paper plan as a flagship plus four orbit papers.
2. Let Paper 1 state programme-wide results while Papers 2–5 contain the proofs or evidence.
3. Route each orbit by its substantive audience rather than by the programme’s general narrative.
4. Keep appendices limited to genuinely subordinate detail.
5. Retain Paper 6 and Paper 7 only after their respective mathematical gates close.
6. If Paper 2 overruns, split by coherent theorem class rather than by “results versus proofs.”
7. Preserve a monograph and/or complete archive as the uncompressed synthesis layer.
